// ── CC OFFSET NOTE — KNOWN, MEASURED, ACCEPTED (operator ruling, 2026-07-28) ──────────
// A back-to-back MATRIX+MATRIX pair IS a Combo Chain by definition. It is also the ONLY
// constituent permutation with no FVG in it: matrix combos are measured on the candle they
// describe (lag 0), so a matrix-matrix pair sits on candles (t-1, t) and its newest candle
// is t. EVERY other permutation contains an FVG combo, whose event is the big displacement
// candle t-1 (the FVG is only confirmable on the candle after it), so those chains have
// t-1 as their newest fully-known candle.
// DECISION: ALL CC marks render at a SINGLE uniform offset -1. We are aware that for the
// pure matrix-matrix case this places the mark on the OLDER candle of the pair, one bar to
// the left of where that chain completed. That is accepted deliberately: one constant
// offset for every CC is simpler and safer than a conditional offset that would have to
// switch per permutation at render time, and the matrix-matrix case is the lone exception
// in an otherwise FVG-bearing set. Do NOT "fix" this into a conditional offset.
// v1.7: MAT+MAT now FIRES here (UC qualifier removed), so this exception is live, not
// hypothetical -- that pair's mark sits on the older of its two candles, by decision.
plotshape(fire_qCC, "CC: Combo Chain Bear", shape.labeldown, location.top, #E5393566, -1, "CC", color.white, size=size.normal)
plotshape(fire_qS29, "S29: 4K + ANY FABLE Bear", shape.square, location.belowbar, #C62828, 0, "4K\n+ANY", color.white, size=size.large)
plotshape(fire_qS31, "S31: NAG + ANY FABLE Bear", shape.cross, location.belowbar, #FF1744B3, 0, "NAG\n+ANY", color.white, size=size.large)
plotshape(fire_qS33, "S33: OPEN1- + ANY FABLE Bear", shape.xcross, location.belowbar, #FF9100, 0, "OPEN1\n+ANY", color.white, size=size.huge)
plotshape(fire_qS35, "S35: DYNAMITE + ANY FABLE Bear", shape.flag, location.belowbar, #F06292B3, -1, "DYN\n+ANY", color.white, size=size.large)
plotshape(fire_qRSA, "R-S + ANY FABLE Bear", shape.arrowdown, location.belowbar, #8E24AA, 0, "R-S\n+ANY", color.white, size=size.large)
plotshape(fire_qRRA, "R-S+R-C + ANY FABLE Bear", shape.triangledown, location.belowbar, #FFAB4066, 0, "R-S+R-C\n+ANY", color.black, size=size.huge)
